# Force LF line endings on files that get baked into Linux Docker images, regardless of the
# committer's OS or local git autocrlf setting. Windows git clients and GitHub's windows-latest
# Actions runner both commonly default to autocrlf=true, which silently rewrites LF to CRLF on
# checkout. A CRLF line ending on a shell script's shebang line (#!/bin/sh\r) makes Linux unable
# to find the interpreter, failing with a confusing "exec ...: no such file or directory" --
# exactly what broke the self-hosted installer's backend/worker containers. See DECISIONS.md.
* text=auto
*.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
Dockerfile.* text eol=lf
docker-compose.yml text eol=lf
*.conf text eol=lf
